# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
# NOTE: no bare `debug` line here. It was unanchored, so it matched a directory named
# `debug` ANYWHERE in the tree — it hid `.planning/debug/` and would have silently hidden
# any `crates/*/src/debug/` source directory from git and from crates.io. That is the
# CB-510 defect (`models/` matching `src/models/`) in CLAUDE.md's Publishing Safety
# section. It was also redundant: cargo's build output is `target/debug`, already covered
# by the `target` rules below (`git check-ignore -v target/debug/apr` cites `target`).
target/
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Coverage artifacts
*.profraw
*.profdata

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Property testing regressions
proptest-regressions/

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
lcov.info

# mdBook generated output
book/book/
*.log

# Shell artifacts (generated by aprender-shell)
crates/aprender-shell/corpus/
crates/aprender-shell/models/
crates/apr-cli/models/
crates/aprender-shell/qa_test_artifacts/

# Model files (downloaded/converted - don't commit large binaries)
*.gguf
*.safetensors
# Synthetic random-init CI fixtures (plan 08-02, `just laya-fixtures`), NOT real weights: exactly
# these two paths, so the tests read the same file format production does. Real checkpoints stay
# under the root-anchored /models/ below and are never committed.
!/crates/aprender-core/tests/fixtures/modernbert_tiny/model.safetensors
!/crates/aprender-decide/tests/fixtures/laya_tiny/checkpoint/model.safetensors
# Root-level .apr files (test fixtures in crates/ are OK)
/*.apr
# Root-level models/ only (NOT src/models/ which is source code)
/models/
/models
# Root-level data/ only (CB-510: root-anchored, never a bare pattern).
# Benchmark preparations (apr data tweet-eval-stance) land here, and the
# original tweet text must never be committed to this repository.
/data/
# CDK deploy project (cargo pmcp): installed deps and synth output only —
# the CDK source (deploy/bin, deploy/lib, cdk.json) is committed.
/deploy/node_modules/
/deploy/cdk.out/
/deploy/.build/
# cargo-pmcp per-checkout state (which named target is active on THIS machine)
/.pmcp/active-target
# ...and the same two per-checkout files under a PER-CRATE .pmcp/ directory.
# CB-510 in reverse: the root-anchored forms above are correctly narrow for the
# root, but `cargo pmcp` also writes state into `crates/<crate>/.pmcp/`, which
# they never matched — so `crates/aprender-mcp-chronos-lambda/.pmcp/active-target`
# and `.../deployment.toml` sat permanently untracked and dirtied every
# clean-tree assertion. Named EXACTLY, not a bare `.pmcp/`: `deploy.toml` and
# `deploy.toml.template` under those same directories ARE curated and tracked.
**/.pmcp/active-target
**/.pmcp/deployment.toml
# insta's pending-snapshot output. Written whenever a snapshot test fails (three
# do on this box, pre-existing) and never committed: 0 of the 23 tracked
# snapshots is a `.snap.new`. Left untracked it dirties the working tree after
# any test run, which is exactly what the cleanroom `--locked` gate asserts against.
**/*.snap.new
.pmat-metrics/
.cargo/config.toml

# PMAT caches and generated data (recursive — covers root AND subcrates)
# CB-510 lesson: non-recursive patterns miss crates/*/.pmat/ files
**/.pmat/

# predict_merge.sh records (BSE-14): a per-branch prediction of whether
# merge(origin/main, HEAD) passes the tree-property guards. Machine-local
# and branch-keyed -- never meant to be committed.
/.predict/
# Artefacts the dogfood protocol creates (skill rule: gitignore all three).
# .pv was TRACKED until #2644's twice-run showed every dogfood run mutates
# contracts.idx/lint-previous.json, flipping the NEXT run's git-clean gate:
# the runner dirtied the tree it then measured (finding TWICE-1; also CI-5 —
# a tracked index is stale by construction, pv regenerates it locally).
**/.dogfood/
**/.pv/
**/.pmat-metrics/
**/.pmat-qa/
**/.pmat-work/

# Generated exports
probar-export/

# Backup files
*.bak
*.cov-backup
.cargo/config.toml.coverage-backup

# PMAT
.pmat/backup/
.pmat/context.idx/
.pmat/workspace.idx/
.pmat/deps-cache.json
src/generated_contracts.rs
crates/apr-cli/trace-*.json
.pv/cache/
**/.pv/cache/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
contracts/.pv/
per-layer-trace/

# Dev-convenience symlinks — must NOT be tracked (publish-safety: tracked
# symlinks break cargo package; see contracts/publish-safety-v1.yaml).
# - aprender-present/contracts -> presentar-core/contracts (only for `pv codegen`;
#   the build uses the checked-in src/generated_contracts.rs)
# - aprender-train/checkpoints -> machine-local /mnt/... (package-excluded)
/crates/aprender-present/contracts
/crates/aprender-train/checkpoints

# Local agent/tooling state — machine-specific, never part of the source tree.
# Root-anchored (CB-510): a bare `gsd/` would also match any src/**/gsd/.
/.gsd/
/.serena/
# `deploy.toml` IS curated and tracked; `deployment.toml` is written by
# `cargo pmcp deploy` on every run and only records the last endpoint.
/.pmcp/deployment.toml

# Phase 5 benchmark working files. Root-anchored per CB-510: the evidence set
# (rows, selections, locks, run-manifest.json) IS committed; the 87 MB-per-cell
# .apr artifacts, per-cell logs, probe text and the driver pid lock are not.
/benchmarks/*/artifacts/
/benchmarks/*/logs/
/benchmarks/*/probe/
/benchmarks/*/.driver.lock
# Python bytecode from scripts/*.py (dogfood gate helpers import each other)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Root-level scratch that was once committed by accident (removed in 0.65.0):
# pmat probe outputs, a stray simulation binary and its source, an 8.9 MB
# strings dump, ticket lists. Root-anchored (CB-510): `/` so src/models is
# never caught by a bare pattern.
/*.out
/remaining*.txt
/gh_strings.txt
/sim4
/sim4.rs
/.lint-cache

# `pmat work` scratch files for docs/roadmaps/roadmap.yaml — never commit
# these; a tracked copy races the real file in every future diff
# (BSE-09a, PMAT-1065, checked by scripts/check_roadmap_sorted.sh).
docs/roadmaps/*.bak
docs/roadmaps/*.lock

# Generated on demand by crates/apr-cli/tests/pixel_regression.rs (28 MB; never commit it --
# a committed copy makes publish_atomically() unreachable, which hid a real race, see #3051)
/crates/apr-cli/playbooks/snapshots/test.apr

# Quorum lane scratch: per-lane stdout/err and the pid file the runner writes.
# The VERDICT artifact (quorum-*.json) is committed; its .lanes/ working
# directory is transient and a lane review correctly refused a PR carrying it.
docs/audits/quorum-*.json.lanes/
